  "notes": "Port census is a stated build, not a fixed chassis figure. Datasheet 'NetEngine 8000 X Series Router' (Port Density table): '400G | Maximum Number of Ports/Board 8 | X16 128 | X8 64 (4T SRU) | X4 32 (4T SRU)' - so 8 x 8 = 64 for the X8 and 8 x 4 = 32 for the X4, 8 x 16 = 128 for the X16, and this entry is that 8-cage card in every line-card slot. The same datasheet's board table lists the card as 'LPUI-4T/LPUI-4T-E/LPUI-4T-L: 8*400GE QSFP-DD + 8*100GE QSFP28', and the X Series brochure gives Service Slots 4 / 8 / 16 and Slot Capability 1T/2T/4T/14.4T/19.2T per slot. Chassis facts from the product page: 346.30 Tbit/s switching, 48848 Mpps forwarding, Main Control Board 2, 1:1, SFU 8, 7+1, Line Card 8, Power Module 10 power modules, N+1, Fan Module 12 fans, 11+1, 703 mm (15.8U) x 442 mm x 874 mm, typical power 11,017 W, weight in full configuration 296.6 kg. Deliberately not claimed: the 8 x 100GE QSFP28 cages that each LPUI-4T also carries (their port numbers inside the mixed-rate card are a physical layout the datasheet does not print, and the hardware guide only works one mixed example - 25GE ports 0-35 then 100GE 36-45 - so a numbering here would be an inference); the 14.4T build (36 x 400GE per card, Port Density row '400G (14.4T SRU)' -> 576 / 288 / 144) and the 40-cage 100GE build (640 / 320 / 160) are different populations, not folded into this entry. Port names follow the hardware guide's rule that NetEngine 8000 X ports are 'slot ID/subcard ID/port number' with a fixed card's subcard ID 0; LPU slots are 1-8 on the X8. No PoE (matches the request) and no console port (none published). MPLS LDP/RSVP-TE/VPLS/L3VPN, SR-MPLS, SRv6, EVPN/VXLAN, FlexE, BNG, CGN, IPsec and 1588v2 are in the datasheet's Product Features but are not engine capability tokens, so they are recorded here rather than declared; CGN is why 'nat' is declared, and no firewall capability is claimed because the vendor's feature table does not list one. Sources read 2026-11-17: https://e.huawei.com/marketingcloud/pep/asset/20000001/Material/f274014bf341427ba955064d5919b2fe/M2T1A669N992206662674575488/NetEngine%208000%20X%20Series%20Universal%20Service%20Router%20Datasheet.pdf (canonical; Port Density + board tables, read via the identical PDF mirrored at https://www.ycict.net/wp-content/uploads/2023/09/NetEngine-8000-X-Series-Universal-Service-Router-Datasheet.pdf because Huawei's host answers 404 to a non-browser fetch); https://e-file.huawei.com/marketingcloud/pep/asset/20000001/Material/02d9fbd0807243b5b37d66759665d25a/M3T1A590N1069280707103375400/NetEngine%208000%20X%20Series%20Brochure.pdf (service slots, LPUI-4T rows, product features); https://e.huawei.com/en/products/routers/ne8000 (per-model switching/forwarding/MPU/SFU/power table); https://support.huawei.com/enterprise/en/doc/EDOC1100465699/67e2f8f8/board (port numbering)."
